  "worked_solution": "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<\u2026<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},\u2026,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since $4.5$ does not belong to $[0,4].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since it does not include the left endpoint $a=4.$\n\n- Statement III is  a partition of  $[0,4].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
